{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And Esau harbored hatred.</b> He harbored hatred; likewise \"they harbored hatred against him\" (Genesis 49:23)." "<b>And Esau said in his heart.</b> It is possible that he revealed his secret to one of his friends, and some say it was by way of prophecy. The first is closer [to the truth]."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's gloss נטר איבה is Aramaic for 'harbored hatred'; translated directly as it is his own explanatory equivalent."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:05.454223972Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}